cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "Arabic Cybersecurity OCR Benchmark"
authors:
  - family-names: Alsumaitti
    given-names: Osamah
date-released: 2026-07-08
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A KITAB-Bench-aligned model-selection study evaluating four vision-language
  models on Arabic cybersecurity documents. 46 books are distilled to a 276-page
  benchmark and scored on CER/WER, chrF, table structure, hallucination,
  robustness, efficiency, and a security-specific IOC layer. Ground truth was
  produced by Claude Opus 4.8 transcription with a light human review.
keywords:
  - OCR
  - Arabic
  - vision-language models
  - benchmark
  - cybersecurity
  - document understanding
